Package: where-is-my-memory
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12), python3-gi, python3-psutil, python3-docker, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5)
Recommends: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator, docker-ce-cli | docker.io, x11-utils
Description: tray monitor for forgotten containers, dev servers and apps
 Where Is My Memory watches the processes and Docker containers of the
 current session and flags those that hold on to memory without being used.
 It lives in the system tray and never acts without confirmation.
